                                    <fo:list-block relative-align="baseline" provisional-label-separation="3pt" provisional-distance-between-starts="40px" space-after="1.33em" space-before="1.33em">
                                        <fo:list-item><fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()"><fo:block text-align="end">1. </fo:block></fo:list-item-label><fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()"><fo:block>This
                                            process applies to all Space plants that have FSC and
                                            PRS technology. Licensee plants should contact their
                                            Space Global Technical Assistance Account Manager. </fo:block></fo:list-item-body></fo:list-item>
                                        <fo:list-item><fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()"><fo:block text-align="end">2. </fo:block></fo:list-item-label><fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()"><fo:block>FSC and
                                            PRS are High Risk Systems obsolescence ranked –
                                            Unsupportable systems. The reason is that most (if not
                                            all) spare parts are not available for those systems.
                                            Plants must rely on in-house inventories, and because of
                                            the age of this equipment, in-house spare parts should
                                            not be considered a reliable solution.</fo:block></fo:list-item-body></fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                            </fo:block>
